groundwright has no third-party runtime dependencies. The golden set is a plain mapping, the
retriever is a callable you pass in, and the engine is the Python standard library only (re).

Extracted from the governed runner at github.com/souzalrns/network-agents-setup
(runner/plan_runner/l5_eval.py). The runner keeps the MCP retriever default and the chunking
used to validate a golden set offline; this package is the standalone, retriever-agnostic
grounding-gate core (the `Retrieve` seam).
